.TH Install-Rclone 1 "December 2025" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Install-Rclone \- Install the latest Rclone release
.SH SYNOPSIS
Install-Rclone [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads and installs the current Rclone release directly from rclone.org. This version is typically newer than the one available in Debian/Ubuntu system repositories. The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Detects system architecture (x86_64, aarch64, armv7l, armv6l, i686, i386)
.IP \(bu 2
Ensures required tools (curl, unzip) are installed
.IP \(bu 2
Downloads the appropriate Rclone binary for the detected platform
.IP \(bu 2
Removes any existing Rclone package installed via apt-get
.IP \(bu 2
Installs the binary to /usr/bin/rclone with correct permissions
.IP \(bu 2
Creates directories /var/lib/rclone and /var/log/rclone
.IP \(bu 2
Installs the man page to /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.IP \(bu 2
Updates the man database
.IP \(bu 2
Cleans up downloaded files
.PP
After installation, use 'rclone selfupdate' to upgrade to newer versions.
.PP
This script must be run with sudo/root privileges.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show usage information and exit.
.SH SUPPORTED ARCHITECTURES
.TP
.B x86_64
Intel/AMD 64-bit (linux-amd64)
.TP
.B aarch64
ARM 64-bit (linux-arm64)
.TP
.B armv7l, armv6l
ARM 32-bit (linux-arm)
.TP
.B i686, i386
Intel/AMD 32-bit (linux-386)
.SH USAGE
.RS
.nf
\fBsudo ./build/Install-Rclone\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success
.TP
1
Error (unsupported architecture, missing dependencies, download failure, etc.)
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B Required:
curl, unzip
.IP
These will be automatically installed via apt-get if missing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/rclone
Rclone binary
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/rclone.1
Rclone man page
.TP
.I /var/lib/rclone
Rclone data directory
.TP
.I /var/log/rclone
Rclone log directory
.TP
.I /sbin/mount.rclone
Symlink to /usr/bin/rclone enabling mount command integration
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rclone (1)
.PP
Rclone homepage: https://rclone.org/
